{"slug":"langley-homes-for-sale","path":"/langley-homes-for-sale.html","url":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/langley-homes-for-sale.html","kind":"page","title":"Langley Homes for Sale | MLS Listings in Langley BC","canonical":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/langley-homes-for-sale.html","seo":{"Title":"Langley Homes for Sale | MLS Listings in Langley BC","Meta description":"Browse Langley homes for sale including houses, townhomes & new listings. View MLS properties in Langley BC with local Realtor Jared Gibbons.\n","H1":"Langley Homes for Sale | MLS Listings","Canonical":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/langley-homes-for-sale.html","Meta robots":"index, follow","OG title":"Langley Homes for Sale | MLS Listings in Langley BC","OG description":"Browse Langley homes for sale including houses, townhomes & new listings. View MLS properties in Langley BC with local Realtor Jared Gibbons.\\n","OG image":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/_media/quick-uploads/dnikbzyufjyo.jpg","Published":"","Modified":""},"blocks":[{"t":"h","level":1,"text":"Langley Homes for Sale | MLS Listings"},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Langley takes in two municipalities, the City of Langley and the Township of Langley, and the listings below cover both: condos and townhomes in Langley City and Willoughby, detached houses in Walnut Grove, Murrayville and Brookswood, and acreages and farms across the Township, where about three-quarters of the land is in the Agricultural Land Reserve. Use the shortcuts below to narrow by home type or price, and see my"},{"t":"Langley neighbourhood guides","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/langley-neighbourhood-guides.html"},{"t":"for schools, parks and what to check before you buy. For current prices and sales, see the"},{"t":"Langley market stats","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/fraser-valley-market-stats.html#langley"},{"t":"."}]},{"t":"grid"},{"t":"h","level":2,"text":"Langley market numbers"},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"The Fraser Valley Real Estate Board (FVREB) reports Langley as one statistics area. Its monthly package doesn't list the City of Langley, Fort Langley, Aldergrove, Walnut Grove or Willoughby separately, so its benchmark prices, median prices, sales and active listings cover the whole Langley area."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"See the latest Langley market numbers","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/fraser-valley-market-stats.html#langley"},{"t":"by home type."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Area-wide figures can differ a lot from any one street or home, so ask me for recent sales in your Langley neighbourhood."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Source: FVREB."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"See the latest numbers","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/fraser-valley-market-stats.html#langley"},{"t":". Benchmark = MLS® Home Price Index benchmark, a modelled typical home."}]},{"t":"h","level":2,"text":"Langley questions buyers ask"},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"What is a typical price for a detached home in Langley?"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"FVREB publishes a monthly benchmark for a typical detached home in Langley. Check the"},{"t":"current Langley detached benchmark","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/fraser-valley-market-stats.html#langley"},{"t":". A benchmark is a modelled estimate of a typical home, so individual homes sell above and below it. Source:"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"latest FVREB statistics package","h":"https://www.fvreb.bc.ca/statistics/"},{"t":"."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Is Langley a buyer's or seller's market?"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"FVREB answers this with the sales-to-active listings ratio: a month's sales divided by the homes for sale at month end. It treats 12% to 20% as balanced. Below 12% favours buyers, and above 20% favours sellers. Detached homes, townhouses and apartments often sit in different ranges, so check the ratio for the type you want to buy."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"See the latest Langley sales and listings by home type","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/fraser-valley-market-stats.html#langley"},{"t":"."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"What is the difference between the City of Langley and the Township of Langley?"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"They are separate municipalities with their own councils. The City of Langley is about 10 square kilometres and was incorporated in 1955 ("},{"t":"City of Langley","h":"https://www.langleycity.ca/community-culture/about-langley-city"},{"t":"). The Township of Langley covers about 316 square kilometres ("},{"t":"Township of Langley","h":"https://www.tol.ca/en/the-township/about-the-township.aspx"},{"t":"). FVREB reports Langley as one statistics area. For a neighbourhood-by-neighbourhood look, see my"},{"t":"Langley neighbourhood guides","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/langley-neighbourhood-guides.html"},{"t":"."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"How much of Langley is farmland, and how does the ALR affect buying?"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"About 75% of the Township of Langley (235 of its 316 square kilometres) is in the Agricultural Land Reserve, according to the"},{"t":"Township of Langley","h":"https://www.tol.ca/en/the-township/about-the-township.aspx"},{"t":". In the ALR, farming is the priority use and non-farm uses are controlled ("},{"t":"Province of BC land use inventory","h":"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/assets/gov/farming-natural-resources-and-industry/agriculture-and-seafood/agricultural-land-and-environment/strengthening-farming/land-use-inventories/tol_lui2010rprt_2013-08-20_final_v2.pdf"},{"t":"). If you're looking at acreage or a farm, check that parcel's ALR status and what the"},{"t":"Agricultural Land Commission","h":"https://www.alc.gov.bc.ca/"},{"t":"allows before you remove subjects. See my"},{"t":"Langley acreages","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/langley-acreages-for-sale.html"},{"t":"and"},{"t":"Langley farms for sale","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/langley-farms-for-sale-acreages-agricultural-land-mls.html"},{"t":"pages."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"How do I find the school catchment for a Langley home?"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Use the"},{"t":"School Locator","h":"https://www.sd35.bc.ca/school-locator"},{"t":"on the Langley School District (SD 35) website and enter the address. The district also publishes"},{"t":"catchment maps","h":"https://www.sd35.bc.ca/catchment-maps"},{"t":"for the current school year, and its registration pages direct families to the locator. If you're unsure, the school board office is at 604-534-7891. Catchments can change, so confirm the exact address before you buy."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"What kinds of homes can I buy in Langley?"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Langley has condos and townhomes, detached houses, duplexes, houses with coach houses, mobile homes, acreages and farms. Browse"},{"t":"houses","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/langley-houses-for-sale.html"},{"t":","},{"t":"townhomes","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/langley-townhomes-for-sale.html"},{"t":","},{"t":"condos","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/langley-condos-for-sale.html"},{"t":","},{"t":"duplexes","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/langley-duplexes-for-sale.html"},{"t":","},{"t":"homes with coach houses","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/langley-houses-with-coach-houses-for-sale.html"},{"t":"and"},{"t":"mobile homes","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/langley-mobile-homes.html"},{"t":", or call me at 604-928-1361 and I'll set up a search for the type and price range you want."}]},{"t":"h","level":2,"text":"Search Langley homes"},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Live MLS® listings, updated daily. Pick a home type, price range or neighbourhood."}]},{"t":"h","level":3,"text":"By home type"},{"t":"list","items":[[{"t":"Houses","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/langley-houses-for-sale.html"}],[{"t":"Townhomes","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/langley-townhomes-for-sale.html"}],[{"t":"Condos","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/langley-condos-for-sale.html"}],[{"t":"Duplexes","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/langley-duplexes-for-sale.html"}],[{"t":"Homes with coach houses","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/langley-houses-with-coach-houses-for-sale.html"}],[{"t":"Mobile homes","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/